%T A400766 148,162,182,193,213,227,247,256,280,292,316,322,346,358,382,385,409,
%U A400766 421,445,451,475,487,511,512,552,580,620,642,682,710,750,769,809,837
%N A400766 Numbers k such that the k-th composition in standard order is an odd-length palindrome. Positions of odd-length palindromes in A066099.
%C A400766 These compositions are counted by A016116.
%C A400766 Odd-length compositions are A000069, counted by A011782.
%C A400766 Palindrome compositions are A400763, counted by A016116.
%C A400766 Even-length palindromes are A400765, counted by A077957.
%C A400766 The k-th composition in standard order (graded reverse-lexicographic, A066099) is obtained by taking the set of positions of 1's in the reversed binary expansion of k, prepending 0, taking first differences, and reversing again. This gives a bijective correspondence between nonnegative integers and integer compositions.
%F A400766 Complement of A400765 in A400763.
%e A400766 The 59-th composition is (1,1,2,1,1), which is an odd-length palindrome, so 59 is in the sequence.
%e A400766 The terms together with corresponding palindromes begin:
%e A400766     1: (1)
%e A400766     2: (2)
%e A400766     4: (3)
%e A400766     7: (1,1,1)
%e A400766     8: (4)
%e A400766    13: (1,2,1)
%e A400766    16: (5)
%e A400766    22: (2,1,2)
%e A400766    25: (1,3,1)
%e A400766    31: (1,1,1,1,1)
%e A400766    32: (6)
%e A400766    42: (2,2,2)
%e A400766    49: (1,4,1)
%e A400766    59: (1,1,2,1,1)
%e A400766    64: (7)
%e A400766    76: (3,1,3)
%e A400766    82: (2,3,2)
%e A400766    94: (2,1,1,1,2)
%e A400766    97: (1,5,1)
%e A400766   109: (1,2,1,2,1)
%t A400766 stc[n_]:=Differences[Prepend[Join @@ Position[Reverse[IntegerDigits[n,2]],1],0]] // Reverse;
%t A400766 Select[Range[0,100],OddQ[Length[stc[#]]] && stc[#]==Reverse[stc[#]]&]
%Y A400766 For binary expansion we have A048700 (even A048701).
%Y A400766 These compositions are counted by A016116.
%Y A400766 For just palindrome compositions we have A400763, counted by A016116.
%Y A400766 The case of even length is A400765, counted by A077957.
%Y A400766 A000005 counts constant compositions, ranks A272919.
%Y A400766 A000740 counts aperiodic compositions, ranks A328594.
%Y A400766 A001969 ranks even-length compositions, counted by A034008
%Y A400766 A006995 gives binary palindromes, complement A154809.
%Y A400766 A011782 counts compositions.
%Y A400766 A059893 reverses standard composition.
%Y A400766 A066099 lists compositions in standard order.
%Y A400766 A098124 counts compositions with max part = length, ranks A389532.
%Y A400766 A238130 and A333755 count compositions by number of maximal runs, partitions A365676.
